\begin_inset Formula $1$
\end_inset 


\layout Standard

For the M/M/1 we assume that arrivals occur as a Poisson process, and service
 times are exponentialy distributed.
 This implies a birth death process with 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda _{k}=\lambda _{k-1}=\lambda $
\end_inset 

, 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu _{k}=\mu _{k-1}=\mu $
\end_inset 

 giving 
\begin_inset Formula \[
P(k)=\frac{\lambda }{\mu }P\left(k-1\right)\]

\end_inset 

 Thus 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
P(k) & = & \left(\frac{\lambda }{\mu }\right)^{k}\\
P(0) & = & \rho ^{k}P(0),
\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

 where we have defined 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho =\frac{\lambda }{\mu }$
\end_inset 

, known as the utilisation factor.
 
\layout Subsection*

Normalisation
\layout Standard

We can find 
\begin_inset Formula $P(0)$
\end_inset 

 by using the normalisation condition 
\begin_inset Formula $\sum _{k=0}^{\infty }P(k)=1$
\end_inset 

, therefore 
\begin_inset Formula \[
1=P(0)\sum _{k=0}^{\infty }\rho ^{k}\]

\end_inset 

 Giving 
\begin_inset Formula \[
P(0)=\frac{1}{\sum _{k=0}^{\infty }\rho ^{k}}\]

\end_inset 

 The series in the denominator converges if 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho <1$
\end_inset 

 (when the birth rate is less than the death rate), 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\sum _{k=0}^{\infty }\rho ^{k}=\frac{1}{1-\rho },\]

\end_inset 

 meaning that 
\begin_inset Formula \[
P(0)=\left(1-\rho \right)\]

\end_inset 

 and allowing us to write down the 
\emph on 
steady state
\emph default 
 probabilities.
 
\begin_inset Formula \[
P(k)=\rho ^{k}\left(1-\rho \right)\]

\end_inset 


\layout Subsection*

Design Issues
\layout Standard

For the design of networks we are interested in the average queue length
 (a design issue) and the average delay (a quality of service issue).
 
\layout Standard

We can use the steady state probabilities, in combination with Little's
 formula, to compute these quantities.
 
\layout Standard

Start by working out average number of customers in system (not the same
 as average queue length).
 
\layout LyX-Code


\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\bar{N} & = & \left\langle k\right\rangle _{P\left(k\right)}\\
 & = & \sum _{k=0}^{\infty }kP\left(k\right)\\
 & = & \left(1-\rho \right)\sum _{k=0}^{\infty }k\rho ^{k}\\
 & = & \rho \left(1-\rho \right)\sum _{k=0}^{\infty }k\rho ^{k-1}\\
 & = & \rho \left(1-\rho \right)\frac{\partial \sum _{k=0}^{\infty }\rho ^{k}}{\partial \rho }\\
 & = & \rho \left(1-\rho \right)\frac{\partial }{\partial \rho }\left[\frac{\rho }{1-\rho }\right]\\
 & = & \rho \left(1-\rho \right)\frac{1}{\left(1-\rho \right)^{2}}\\
 & = & \frac{\rho }{1-\rho }\\
 & = & \frac{\lambda }{\mu -\lambda }
\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


